  "arm_meanings": {
    "teacher": "Public full embedding teacher; 40 January GT rows/class, February selection",
    "A": "Public lookup initialization; manual GT + extra hard teacher labels",
    "B": "Public lookup initialization; manual GT/extra hard teacher labels + soft teacher probabilities",
    "C": "Public lookup initialization; all 200/class GT only",
    "D": "Public lookup initialization; all GT + soft teacher probabilities",
    "E": "Public lookup initialization; all GT + extra hard teacher labels + soft teacher probabilities",
    "S": "Fully random compact classifier, all 200/class GT; no teacher weights, labels or data selection",
    "L": "Fully random compact classifier, only 40/class GT, repeated to equal updates",
    "P": "Public lookup initialization, only 40/class GT, repeated to equal updates"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "diverse15 contains 14 single-provider categories and a five-provider DoH aggregate, not 15 strictly independent vendors",
    "diverse20 adds five Facebook/Microsoft sibling categories to diverse15; Google subdivision appears only in google20",
    "Class cohorts are different tasks, not a causal isolation of provider similarity",
    "Benchmark curator uses known class membership for identical balanced input selection in all arms; A/B hide extra labels only during optimization, not a strict end-to-end annotation-cost claim",
    "Classes/sample counts fixed from January/February availability before new model scores",
    "Macro-F1 and per-class confusion are primary; shared-six-service performance is reported across all four tasks",
    "Same input IDs for 5/30 packets; unique first-five-packet input/label pairs; cross-label ambiguities retained",
    "February and March exclude first-five-packet matches from earlier months, a conditional novel-input cohort",
    "March has been studied in prior project work; this is retrospective temporal evaluation, not a globally untouched final test",
    "All arms match occurrences and updates within a cohort; compute grows with class count",
    "200 unique rows/class is lower than previous 800-row experiments because minor services lack support",
    "Every selected row repeated eight times; manual rows retain GT in every arm",
    "Fixed architecture and inherited hyperparameters are a benchmark, not a guarantee of each method best possible performance",
    "MPS is not bitwise deterministic"
  ]
}
